WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:05.070
It's rare to find a movie project that doesn't
accrue a thousand-thespian-long conga line

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.020
during casting.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.300
But these are the roles that some really famous
actors rejected.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.240
It seems like no one in Hollywood wanted these
parts!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.520
The true hallmark of an actor's actor is the
kind who only does a movie because of an unshakable

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.940
interest in their character's transformation
over the course of a narrative.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.240
But The Notebook's Noah Calhoun has none of
that growth.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.010
He begins the movie in love with the pretty
blonde girl and ends up in love with the same

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:33.660
pretty blonde girl, making the role an unattractive
one for most "serious" actors.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.420
This prompted most thespians to pass on the
part, at least according to Nicholas Sparks,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:40.600
the author of the novel that the film was
based on.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.280
This left the door wide open for Ryan Gosling
to slide in and win over the world's heart

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.000
in a single romantic chick flick.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.140
What do Michelle Pfeiffer, Meg Ryan, and Laura
Dern all have in common?

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:56.260
It turns out these three actresses were all
once on the short list for the part of Clarice

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.299
Starling, a role we now firmly associate with
Jodie Foster thanks to her amazing performance

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.649
in The Silence of the Lambs.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.480
But Foster only got the part because Pfeiffer
and Ryan rejected the script with extreme

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.000
prejudice due to a shared distaste for the
film's violent and disturbed nature, which

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.880
director Jonathan Demme revealed at an Austin
Film Festival interview.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.040
"So um the script goes to Meg Ryan.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.880
And uh word comes back very quickly like 'good
God I could never do a movie like that.'

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.240
She was slightly offended."

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:29.399
While Demme wanted Dern for the part, she
was relatively unknown at the time.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.840
So he ultimately went with Foster, at the
gentle behest of the studio.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.660
If you thought The Lord of the Rings had a
substantial lack of Nicolas Cage in it, you're

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:38.600
not the only one.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.340
Director Peter Jackson thought Aragorn would
be perfectly portrayed by none other than

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.300
everyone's favorite National Treasure.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:50.460
And Jackson also thought that Russell Crowe
would fit Aragorn's lofty role equally well.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.600
Also crossing Jackson's mind as the perfect
Aragorn was none other than Daniel Day-Lewis.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.600
As you can tell, Jackson had a lengthy wish
list of actors for this role, but that list

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.440
didn't include Viggo Mortensen, the guy who
ultimately landed the part.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.840
As for why the previously mentioned actors
didn't work out, Cage didn't want franchise

00:02:09.849 --> 00:02:14.680
obligations to distract from time with his
kids, Crowe had prior commitments, and Day-Lewis

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.400
never publicly stated his reason.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.640
Thankfully, Mortensen pulled off the job just
fine.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.240
When all is said and done, the real heroes
of the Fifty Shades franchise are the casting

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:25.740
directors.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.740
They're the brave souls who had to wade through
the bowels of Hollywood to find a pair of

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.080
actors willing to denigrate themselves for
the adaptations of one of the most embarrassing

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.960
novel trilogies of all time.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.450
Fifty Shades of Grey was always destined to
be a kinky test in pain tolerance, if that

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.920
pain was derived from permanent career embarrassment.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:48.140
The actors who couldn't reject the role of
billionaire sadist Christian Grey fast enough

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.450
included Charlie Hunnam, Garrett Hedlund,
and Ryan Gosling.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.280
"Any chance of Fifty Shades of Grey?

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:54.280
Everybody wants to know."

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.319
"I have no, what is this book that everyone's
talking about it seems very popular."

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:02.730
As for the submissive end of the casting spectrum,
the actresses who weren't too keen on playing

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:06.820
Anastasia Steele include Lucy Hale, Chloe
Bridges, and Emma Watson.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.080
The fight for who would get the role of Michael
Corleone was actually a rather small scuffle,

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.900
fought mainly between director Francis Ford
Coppola and his studio overheads.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.230
The studio petitioned hard for actors like
Martin Sheen and Jack Nicholson, but after

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:24.890
Nicholson turned down the part and Coppola
stood his ground, the studio was forced to

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.040
entertain his desire to cast Al Pacino.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:32.079
In a 2004 interview with Movieline, Nicholson
explained his decision by saying,

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:37.060
"Back then I believed that Indians should
play Indians and Italians should play Italians."

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:41.180
Nicholson's sentiment turned out well for
the film, but even Pacino didn't originally

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:41.980
want the part.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:46.860
He knew that nobody wanted to cast him except
for Coppola, whom Pacino thought was "a bit

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.360
mad."

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:50.250
Luckily Pacino and the studio both came around.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:56.060
Similar to Fifty Shades of Grey, Twilight
is another case of an embarrassing book turning

00:03:56.060 --> 00:04:00.180
into an embarrassing movie that no one wanted
to embarrass themselves by starring in.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.800
Thus, a list of actresses who rejected the
role of Bella Swan is no surprise.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:09.680
That list includes Emily Browning, Frances
Bean Cobain, and Emmy Rossum.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.220
Their reasons ranged from general disinterest
to downright offense at how bad the script

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.720
was.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:19.160
Considering how the poorly-received finished
product turned out, one can only imagine how

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:22.480
grateful they must be for their past selves'
well-warranted foresight.

